why is every image I upload larger than the frame/border it is supposed to be\
There are 
\f2\b two reasons
\f1\b0 , and one of them is a real syntax problem in your current CSS.\
First, an 
\f3\fs26 <img>
\f1\fs24  does 
\f2\b not automatically obey the visual size of its parent frame
\f1\b0 . If you upload a 2000\'d71500 image, the browser knows the image is large unless you explicitly tell it:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 width: 100%;\
height: 100%;\
object-fit: cover;\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 The border/frame and the image are two separate elements. Setting a frame to 
\f3\fs26 150px \'d7 118px
\f1\fs24  does not by itself resize the 
\f3\fs26 <img>
\f1\fs24  inside it.\
But in your current stylesheet, there is also a more important problem: your 
\f3\fs26 .work-thumb \{
\f1\fs24  block is missing its closing 
\f3\fs26 \}
\f1\fs24  before 
\f3\fs26 .work-thumb img \{
\f1\fs24 .\
You currently effectively have:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 .work-thumb \{\
  width: 100%;\
  height: 260px;\
  overflow: hidden;\
  position: relative;\
  background: var(--panel);\
\
/* missing \} here */\
\
.work-thumb img \{\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 It needs to be:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 .work-thumb \{\
  width: 100%;\
  height: 260px;\
  overflow: hidden;\
  position: relative;\
  background: var(--panel);\
\}\
